<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pago Pago</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pago Pago is the main town and harbour of American Samoa, on one of the finest natural harbours in the South Pacific, on the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tutuila">Tutuila</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> acquired coaling rights there in 1878 and established a naval station in 1900, which administered the territory until 1951. Its economy depends on tuna canning and government services.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pago-pago.jpg" alt="Pago Pago" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NOAA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AmericanSamoaLegislatureBuilding.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
